 a type of recurrent neural network used for processing time-series data. They consist of a large, fixed-size, randomly connected hidden layer called the \"reservoir,\" which processes input data. The weights of the reservoir are typically fixed, and only the output weights are trained. Training involves adjusting the output weights to map the reservoir's states to the desired output. Reservoirs are often trained using random initialization and do not require backpropagation through time, making them computationally efficient.\n\nSummarizing the arXiv papers, none directly match the query \"echo state networks for anomaly detection.\" The closest matches are about graph neural networks and LLMs for anomaly detection, which do not involve ESNs.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":1060,"prompt_eval_duration":44935000,"total_duration":1775881600}}